{"number":334,"title":"DESIGN.md trade-offs: delivery mode is now a security knob; name the vendored mount&#39;s supply-chain improvement","body":"From a design review of `mount/DESIGN.md` (#315). Doc-only.

**The improvement (worth recording as a design benefit):** the vendored mount closes a real supply-chain exposure — consumers previously executed an unauthenticated, unpinned `codeload` tarball at every session start *and on every Bash call* (the PreToolUse guard). Post-flip, consumers execute only code committed in their own history: diffs reviewable, rollback = revert the nightly&#39;s commit.

**The residual (worth a sentence in §10):** for `push`-delivery members, the nightly is an unreviewed fleet-wide code-write channel into `main`; `pr` delivery buys a human review gate on the entire supply chain. That makes `maintenance.delivery` a **security decision**, not just a workflow preference — a member holding secrets or deploy credentials may reasonably choose `pr` for that reason alone. (The preferences fetch remains the one session-time fetch: fail-soft prose, not executed code — acceptable residue, worth naming as such.)","state":"open","html_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/334","user":{"login":"missingbulb","id":73882448,"profile_url":"https://github.com/missingbulb","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73882448?v=4"},"author_association":"OWNER","labels":["quick-win"],"comments":5,"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"created_at":"2026-07-18T19:49:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T05:18:55Z","has_parent":false,"has_children":false,"closed_by_pull_requests":{"total_count":0,"references":[]}}

